      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the consideration, I think it should work. But if the main concern is the memory usage, we can refactor the existing getAllUniqueRecords() to\n```\nint countUniqueRecords(String[] name) {\n}\n```\n\nAnd calls it for all names in the answers. It\u0027s still O(N * M) time complexity, where N is the question number and M is the record / service number.\n\nI am a bit concerned that your proposal looks harder to follow and maintain:\n1. it\u0027s a bit tricky that the NSEC addition depends on the order of the nested for loops and we need to document and maintain it. It looks more straight-forward that we deal with it after all answers have been added\n2. It depends on the implicit invariant you mentioned in another comment, though I think the invariant stands\n3. It now requires 3 calls to `addNsecRecordsForUniqueNames` while my solution needs 2\n\nAfter all, this case is just a \"MAY\" in the spec, I doubt it\u0027s useful and worths the code here. Does mDNSResponder support this \"MAY\"?",
